  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 245 PM EST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nIt is a very pleasant day across the region, with plenty of sunshine \nand temps in the upper 60s and around 70. There is some breezy winds \nthough, with obs showing SW winds gusting up to 20-25 mph this \nafternoon. These winds will relax by this evening as we lose our \nmixing. \n\nA weak cold front will slide through the area tomorrow, bringing low \nstratus clouds but not much of a rain chance. This front will lack \nany deep substantial moisture, though the SPC REFS 1-hour QPF \nprobability for 0.01\" tomorrow is mainly 10-20% for central KY, and \ncloser to 30-40% for the Bluegrass region. Certainly not very high \nprobs for measurable precip tomorrow, but soundings support maybe \nseeing some drizzle or very light rain for LEX and surrounding areas \nin our east. Highs for tomorrow could be slightly tricky to nail \ndown due to the timing of the frontal passage, but generally expect \nupper 50s to lower 60s tomorrow. \n\nCold air advection takes over in the wake of the front, and will \nusher in cooler temps for the weekend. Both Saturday and Sunday \nmornings will feature chances for frost or freeze, with Sunday \nmorning showing the greatest probs for a freeze with lows in the \nupper 20s. There is high confidence in the need for frost/freeze \nheadlines over the weekend, but we are still a little too far out to \nissue one on this forecast package. NBM probs for temps less than \n32F are rather high for Sunday morning, with the entire area at \nleast 50%, but upwards of 85-90% for Lexington and the I-75 \ncorridor. \n\nThe upper flow regime takes on a more zonal component into next \nweek, which keeps our weather dry and uneventful. Daily highs in the \n60s expected next week, with chilly temps each morning. Next precip \nchance may not come until next Thursday, but even that is a low \nchance at this time.",
